# Public-safe append-only feedback log. Do not add personal or secret material.
2026-10-16 - Remove identifying raw benchmark artifacts before public commits/pushes, including their Git history; keep run output private/ignored and publish only reviewed aggregate findings. Persist this rule in AGENTS.repo.md.
2026-10-16 - Treat this repository as public: ignore artifacts containing sensitive information, keep them private, and never force-add them to public commits. Record this rule in AGENTS.repo.md.
2026-10-15 - Address the user as "Sire" in chat; persist the preference in AGENTS.repo.md.
2026-10-20 - Put commit and push confirmation at both the top and bottom of delivery replies, including the commit hash and push destination; end with the confirmation so pushed status is immediately visible. Only confirm successful operations actually performed or verified.
2026-10-20 - Include the full Git commit message (subject and body) plus a brief summary of the committed changes in the bottom commit confirmation; retain the hash and actual push status.
2026-10-20 - Always copy newer local managed-file changes into this repository before applying configuration; preserve templates, unrelated repo edits, and the existing secret/machine-local exclusions.
2026-10-20 - End delivery summaries with any skipped checks and material risks, then the bold commit hash and actual push status/destination, followed by a final "Full commit message:" line containing the recorded Conventional Commit subject (and body when present). Follow this order rather than repeating the status after the message; never imply an unperformed commit or push.
2026-10-21 - Whenever i3 configuration changes, after successful rf (refresh-config), validate the deployed i3 config, reload i3, and verify the affected live behavior before completion; keep this rule in AGENTS.repo.md.
2026-10-22 - Repeated i3 reloads and live window/workspace test moves are disorienting. Prefer read-only checks and isolated displays; batch necessary activation reloads and avoid active-desktop validation that changes focus or bar layout.
2026-10-22 - When asked to create a new GitHub repository, also set it as the working repository's remote (origin unless another name is specified), verify the URL, and keep the working checkout rather than silently switching to a separate copy.
2026-10-22 - For task handoffs, prefer reversed summary paragraph order: verification/results and evidence first, usage or restore instructions next, and the implementation/change summary last. Keep runnable verification commands together in a collapsible details block when included; preserve their execution order.
2026-10-22 - Task-completion handoffs must start with exactly three visible direct verification commands, each immediately followed by its labeled expected-output block, then use the summary paragraph order Verified, Use, Implemented. Keep commands in execution order outside collapsible details; put verification evidence/risks in Verified and the change summary last. This supersedes the earlier collapsible-command preference.
2026-10-22 - Permit home-directory paths, Git author/committer identities, and ordinary recovery-named code/docs in commit privacy checks. Continue blocking authentication secrets, private archives, and explicit private-policy matches.
